        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Legends of the Fall, 1979 novella\n- People: Jim Harrison, James Harrison\n- Places: Montana\n- Topics: family, nature, history, war, love, American literature\n\nFacts:\n- The film Legends of the Fall is based on the 1979 novella of the same title by Jim Harrison.\n- Legends of the Fall is about three brothers and their father living in the wilderness and plains of Montana in the early 20th century.\n- Legends of the Fall depicts how the lives of the brothers and their father are affected by nature, history, war, and love.\n- James Harrison was born on December 11, 1937, and died on March 26, 2016.\n- James Harrison was an American writer known for poetry, fiction, reviews, essays about the outdoors, and writings about food.\n- Jim Harrison was the author of the 1979 novella Legends of the Fall.",
